# Line endings for a repository authored on Windows but consumed as source.
#
# Several payloads here get copied into an OpenWrt build tree, where CRLF is
# not a cosmetic problem - it is a hard failure:
#   * a CR in a shell script shows up as '$\r': command not found
#   * dtc rejects CR characters inside DTS
#   * a CR at the end of a Makefile recipe line breaks the recipe
#
# Force LF for anything meant to be executed or compiled, no matter what the
# local core.autocrlf says.

# Patch payloads - must be byte-applyable.
upstream/**          text eol=lf

# Device trees and build files.
*.dts                text eol=lf
*.dtsi               text eol=lf
*.mk                 text eol=lf

# Shell (both on the build host and on the device itself).
*.sh                 text eol=lf
scripts/board.d/*    text eol=lf

# Never normalise these - they are byte-exact artefacts, and converting a
# binary file corrupts it silently.
*.dtb                binary
*.bin                binary
*.img                binary
*.tar                binary
*.gz                 binary
*.xz                 binary
*.squashfs           binary
*.ipk                binary

# Screenshots.
*.png                binary
*.jpg                binary
*.jpeg               binary
